# Security headers for every response. Nitro also emits an /assets/* caching
# rule into .output/public/_headers at build time; both sets end up in the
# deployed file, so keep this to rules nitro does not set itself.
#
# No Content-Security-Policy here on purpose: the app inlines its own hydration
# script and loads Google Fonts, so a policy written blind would break the site
# rather than protect it. Worth adding deliberately, with the report-only
# header first.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
